{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-ii.3.1:000019:note_appended:bob-cli-ii.3.1.1:1fea640ecaa46dabc6dc9ce775fe8cd0ebb70eeca43ae9d85cb56de690e6b5ab","timestamp":"2026-11-07T23:40:06Z","actor":"bob-cli-ii.3.1.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-ii.3.1.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Membership landed in src/native/gmail/sync/{mod,enroll,scan}.rs plus a shared src/native/gmail/vault_walk.rs (link -a's walk factored out; link.rs now uses it, its regression tests kept in place). API for later phases: sync::ThreadKey (lowercase account + lowercase hex id; index_key() matches MailIndex.by_identity); enroll::EnrollmentFold::load (cross-host gmail.pulled/filed/adopted fold, writer order, bounded malformed-line/event warnings; is_enrolled/origin Legacy|Sync -> already_pulled|already_filed/records/latest with note, task_file, via, route); enroll::append(vault, host, &EnrollmentEvent::{Filed{via: Route|Inbox|Problem, route?}, Adopted}) writes body-free values; scan::scan_watching_tasks(vault, mail_folder, &MailIndex) -> WatchScan {tasks(): path, 1-based line, exact text, block_id, status, targets[{key, note, placement TaskLine|ChildBullet{line}}]; watchers(key), threads(), warnings()}; enroll::Membership::new(&fold, &scan).decide(key) -> Enrolled(origin)|Adopt(AdoptionIntent)|File, adoptions(account) (label-free, from the local scan, per child plan), watched(account). Scan/decide never write; apply phase owns appends. Unused-API allowances are per-item cfg_attr(not(test), allow(dead_code)) for the command phase to remove; journal::pulled_identities/append_pulled stay for old pull until dispatch switches. Note for land/command: per the child plan, adoptions() adopts any open-task-linked unenrolled mail note of the account, including hand-linked notes that never carried the label. Verified: 20 new sync tests + 2 vault_walk tests; cargo test --lib (5547 passed); gmail_pull_attach, gmail_shell, gmail_search_peek, gmail_compose_contract, gmail_draft, gmail_send integration tests pass; cargo fmt --check clean; just lint clean (only pre-existing non-gated warnings)."}}
